---
const faq = [
    {
        q: "What blogs or frontends are supported?",
        a: `Any website that uses markdown files is supported. Here's a short list of popular tools:
        <a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank" class="text-secondary-content underline">Astro</a>,
        <a href="https://gohugo.io/" target="_blank" class="text-secondary-content underline">Hugo</a>,
        <a href="https://jekyllrb.com/" target="_blank" class="text-secondary-content underline">Jekyll</a>,
        <a href="https://www.mkdocs.org/" target="_blank" class="text-secondary-content underline">MkDocs</a>,
        <a href="https://docusaurus.io/" target="_blank" class="text-secondary-content underline">Docusaurus</a>,
        <a href="https://www.gatsbyjs.com/" target="_blank" class="text-secondary-content underline">Gatsby</a>,
        <a href="https://hexo.io/" target="_blank" class="text-secondary-content underline">Hexo</a>,
        <a href="https://vuepress.vuejs.org/" target="_blank" class="text-secondary-content underline">VuePress</a>.
        `,
    },
    {
        q: "How is this different from Decap or similar tools?",
        a: `Unlike most CMS tools, our platform doesn’t require any complex configuration for data ingestion. It’s a fully hosted, headless CMS that integrates directly with your GitHub repo. 
        Similar tools like <a href="https://decapcms.org/" target="_blank" class="text-secondary-content underline">Decap</a> require setup or self-hosting, while we handle everything for you—just connect your repo, and you're all set.`,
    },
    {
        q: "Can I add it to my current site?",
        a: `Absolutely! As long as your site's code is hosted on GitHub, no setup is required to start using the CMS.`,
    },
    {
        q: "How long does it take to set up?",
        a: `Less than 1 minute. Just connect your GitHub repo, and you're ready to go.`,
    },

    {
        q: "Does it work with private repositories?",
        a: `Yes, of course! Your data can remain private. When you grant us access to your private GitHub repository, our CMS will still be able to read and edit your files securely, just like with public repos.`,
    },
    {
        q: "Do you save my data?",
        a: `No... mostly. We only store your account information for login purposes. All your content remains in your GitHub repo. Any edits made through the CMS are pushed directly to your repo, and changes made outside the CMS are synced the next time you log in.`,
    },
    {
        q: "How does this integrate into my build process?",
        a: `Seamlessly! Our tool pushes changes to your repo, triggering your existing GitHub Actions or build pipeline just like a regular commit.`,
    },
    {
        q: "Can I roll back changes?",
        a: `Yes! Since all changes are pushed to your GitHub repo, you can use Git's version control features to roll back to any previous state.`,
    },
    {
        q: "Is this really free?",
        a: `Yes! By leveraging GitHub’s free tier and free hosting services like GitHub Pages or Cloudflare Pages, you can run your blog or site at no cost.`,
    },
    {
        q: "Do I need to know how to code or use markdown?",
        a: `Not at all! Our WYSIWYG editor makes creating and editing content easy, even if you’ve never used markdown or written a single line of code.`,
    },
];
---

<style>
    details[open] summary .icon-expand {
        transform: rotate(180deg);
    }
</style>

<div class="container mx-auto p-4">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">
        <i class="text-4xl bx bx-question-mark text-primary"></i>
        Frequently Asked Questions
    </h1>

    <div class="space-y-2">
        {
            faq.map((qa) => (
                <details class="collapse bg-base-200">
                    <summary class="collapse-title text-xl font-medium">
                        <div class="flex flex justify-between items-center flex-row">
                            {qa.q}
                            <svg
                                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                class="h-6 w-6 icon-expand transition-transform duration-200
                                text-accent"
                                fill="none"
                                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                                stroke="currentColor"
                            >
                                <path
                                    stroke-linecap="round"
                                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                                    stroke-width="2"
                                    d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"
                                />
                            </svg>
                        </div>
                    </summary>
                    <div class="collapse-content" set:html={qa.a} />
                </details>
            ))
        }
    </div>
</div>
